{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS001340","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Selected PGS001340 (snpnet) because it is a direct endpoint match to atrial fibrillation (EFO: atrial fibrillation; phenotyping_reported: Atrial fibrillation) and, per the performance-metrics guidance, it reports PRS-comparable metrics (PGS AUROC no covariates ≈0.613 and PGS R2 no covariates ≈0.023) rather than only covariate-inflated full-model discrimination. Its validation sample size is substantial (n=24,905, European), and the incremental/full-model metrics are provided transparently.

Heritability sanity-check: local EUR h2 records for atrial fibrillation are modest (observed h2 ~0.02–0.03; liability h2 varies by definition, e.g., ~0.055–0.20 depending on phenotype/ascertainment). The reported PGS-only R2 (~0.023) is plausible relative to these h2 estimates (i.e., not exceeding a reasonable genetic-variance ceiling), supporting that the metric is likely on an interpretable scale.

Why not the seemingly higher full-model C-index candidates (e.g., PGS005168): those are heavily influenced by clinical covariates (e.g., CHARGE-AF) and do not provide PRS-only discrimination, making cross-model PRS ranking less reliable per the performance-metrics section."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS001263","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Endpoint fidelity: Target is atrial flutter. Per trait-label guidance, phenotyping_reported is primary; PGS001263 has phenotyping_reported="Atrial flutter" and trait_efo="atrial flutter", making it the cleanest direct match versus the other candidates that bundle atrial fibrillation + flutter or use a time-to-event composite.

Performance/validation package: In European validation (n=24,905), PGS001263 reports PGS-only AUROC 0.617 and PGS-only R² 0.025, with incremental AUROC 0.0217 over covariates—comparable or slightly better than the closest composite alternative (PGS001339) and more directly aligned to the target than the portability-paper scores (PGS001841/PGS002050) that only report partial correlation and do not provide directly comparable AUROC/R² here.

Heritability sanity-check: Local EUR h2 records for closely matching ICD10 I48 (atrial fibrillation and flutter) show observed-scale h2 ~0.015–0.021 (liability h2 ~0.145–0.204). A PGS-only R² ~0.025 for a closely related flutter endpoint is plausible in magnitude (not obviously inflated by covariates), supporting that the reported PRS-only signal is credible."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS002036","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Target trait is depressive disorder; the most endpoint-faithful candidates are those with trait_efo/phenotyping matching depressive disorder / major depressive disorder. Several candidates are not appropriate despite high-looking metrics because their phenotyping is off-target (e.g., PGS000767 is for bilateral putamen volume; PGS000907 is for muscle pain in fluoxetine takers), consistent with the skill guidance to prioritize endpoint fidelity before metrics (read_skill_section: skill_overview) and to treat full-model/packaged metrics cautiously (read_skill_section: performance_metrics).

Among the on-target depression/MDD scores, PGS002036 (LDpred2) from the UKB portability study provides a clean, PRS-focused performance signal (partial correlation partial-r=0.0556 in EUR; n=17,764; basic covariates) and uses a modern genome-wide method with large variant coverage (807,338). Competing direct-endpoint options either report only full-model AUROC/R2 from minimal-phenotyping constructs (PGS000138-145), have unclear/unknown covariates (PGS003333), are effect-size-only without clear PRS-comparable metrics here (PGS002759), or have smaller/less directly comparable evidence.

Heritability sanity-check: local EUR h2 records for depressive disorder/MDD include h2≈0.18 for major depressive disorder (get_heritability_records), making the observed partial-r magnitude for PGS002036 plausible (well below the heritability ceiling) and not suggestive of metric inflation."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS001792","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Target trait is glaucoma; several candidates are direct-label glaucoma or closely aligned POAG/open-angle glaucoma. Per the PRS evaluation guidance (prs_model_evaluator skill_overview + performance_metrics), prioritize endpoint fidelity plus PRS-comparable metrics (PGS-only / covariates-regressed-out) over full-model AUROC that may be covariate-driven.

PGS001792 (Primary open-angle glaucoma; PRS-CS-auto) provides a PRS-comparable metric: Nagelkerke R2 with covariates regressed out = 0.03209, alongside a large European validation sample (n=347,396) and a modern genome-wide Bayesian method with very large variant count (~911k). Competing UKB-framework snpnet scores (PGS001321/1322/1323) report PGS-only R2 of ~0.015–0.022 and modest PGS-only AUROC (~0.60–0.62), while some other candidates report only full-model AUROC (e.g., PGS000137) or only OR without clear PRS-only discrimination.

Heritability sanity-check (get_heritability_records for glaucoma) shows EUR h2 estimates vary by phenotype definition; for open-angle glaucoma, liability-scale h2 is ~0.17–0.21 in GWAS Atlas records, making a PRS-only/covariates-regressed-out R2 around 0.03 plausible and not suspiciously inflated. Overall, PGS001792 has the strongest combination of (i) glaucoma-relevant endpoint, (ii) PRS-comparable performance evidence, and (iii) large-scale validation and genome-wide method."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS004163","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Trait/endpoint alignment: PGS004163 is explicitly for rheumatoid arthritis (trait_efo: rheumatoid arthritis) and its phenotyping_reported is seropositive RA, which is a clinically coherent RA endpoint (per trait-label guidance: phenotyping_reported is primary; subtype endpoints can still be strong matches for a generic disease target when coherent and well-supported). Competing candidates include juvenile idiopathic arthritis and other inflammatory arthritides (endpoint mismatch), and some RA scores with weaker/less comparable metrics.

Performance/validation evidence: Within the large, internally consistent 2023 Am J Hum Genet evaluation set (same evaluation N=90,274; covariates listed as 0, reducing covariate-packaging concerns), PGS004163 has the strongest reported discrimination and variance explained among the RA candidates shown (full_model_auc ~0.747; R2 ~0.138), outperforming other method variants like LDpred2.CV (PGS004049; AUC ~0.728; R2 ~0.122). Earlier UKB snpnet RA models (PGS001310/PGS001309) show notably lower AUC (~0.665) and PGS-only R2 (~0.015).

Heritability sanity-check: Local EUR h2 records for rheumatoid arthritis show non-trivial SNP-heritability in external GWAS resources (e.g., h2 ~0.13–0.17 in GWAS Atlas RA records), supporting that an RA PRS can explain meaningful variance; the observed R2 values in the chosen model are directionally plausible given this ceiling, while very high full-model metrics in small/packaged settings would warrant more skepticism."}

{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS000461","confidence":"Moderate","rationale":"Endpoint fidelity: PGS000461 is a direct match to the target (trait_reported/trait_efo/phenotyping_reported all “Squamous cell carcinoma”), whereas several other candidates are for esophageal cancer or other squamous cell carcinoma sites (head/neck, lung) or a restricted survivorship endpoint (PGS005209), which trait-label guidance treats as weaker for generic disease-risk deployment.

Performance evidence (noting these are full-model metrics with covariates): among the direct SCC models, PGS000461 has the strongest reported discrimination and effect size package (full-model AUROC 0.599 with Nagelkerke R² 0.0304; OR 1.49 per SD and OR 3.51 for top 1% vs rest). It is also competitive with the other direct SCC options (e.g., PGS000120 AUROC 0.59; PGS000463 AUROC 0.593; UKB-trained PGS000462/464/466/468 AUROC ~0.57–0.575). PGS000731 has slightly higher AUROC (0.605) but has unknown covariates and no training N reported, making the evidence package less clean.

Heritability sanity-check: local EUR h2 records for self-reported squamous cell carcinoma show low observed-scale h2 (~0.0017–0.0032) but materially higher liability-scale h2 (~0.13–0.23). This supports interpreting modest AUROC/R² values as plausible for SCC and does not contradict selecting the best-performing direct-endpoint model in this candidate set."}
